From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: give the firmware the user's country again after a
 restart

A country set through a user hint (hostapd's country_code) reaches the
firmware once, as WMI_INIT_COUNTRY from the regulatory notifier. After a
firmware restart the host still holds that regulatory domain, but the
firmware is back on the country of its board data and nothing sends it
the user's again: only chips with current_cc_support get their country
back in reconfig_complete. An Archer AX55 v1 set to PL came out of a
recovery reporting 19 dBm on 5 GHz instead of 22.

Send the init country again when a radio whose country a user hint has
set is started after a restart, before its interfaces come up: sent from
reconfig_complete the firmware takes the country, but the vdevs already
running keep the power they were started with.

From kuncy7/openwrt-nss-edma (999-9966, ipq50xx-2026.10.12).

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -6808,6 +6808,12 @@ static int ath11k_mac_op_start(struct ieee80211_hw *hw)
 
 	/* TODO: Do we need to enable ANI? */
 
+	/* before the interfaces come up again: a running vdev keeps the
+	 * transmit power of the country it was started under
+	 */
+	if (ar->state == ATH11K_STATE_RESTARTED)
+		ath11k_reg_restore_user_cc(ar);
+
 	ath11k_reg_update_chan_list(ar, false);
 
 	ar->num_started_vdevs = 0;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
@@ -974,6 +974,37 @@ void ath11k_reg_free(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 	}
 }
 
+/* A restarted firmware is back on the country of its board data, while the
+ * regulatory domain a user hint had set lives on in the host. Give the
+ * firmware that country again; without current_cc_support nothing else does.
+ */
+void ath11k_reg_restore_user_cc(struct ath11k *ar)
+{
+	struct wmi_init_country_params init_country_param = {};
+	const struct ieee80211_regdomain *regd;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (ar->ab->hw_params.current_cc_support || !ar->regdom_set_by_user)
+		return;
+
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	regd = rcu_dereference(ar->hw->wiphy->regd);
+	if (!regd) {
+		rcu_read_unlock();
+		return;
+	}
+	memcpy(init_country_param.cc_info.alpha2, regd->alpha2, 2);
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
+	init_country_param.flags = ALPHA_IS_SET;
+
+	ret = ath11k_wmi_send_init_country_cmd(ar, init_country_param);
+	if (ret)
+		ath11k_warn(ar->ab,
+			    "failed to set the country again after the restart: %d\n",
+			    ret);
+}
+
 int ath11k_reg_set_cc(struct ath11k *ar)
 {
 	struct wmi_set_current_country_params set_current_param = {};
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.h
@@ -47,4 +47,5 @@ int ath11k_reg_handle_chan_list(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 				struct cur_regulatory_info *reg_info,
 				enum ieee80211_ap_reg_power power_type);
 int ath11k_reg_set_cc(struct ath11k *ar);
+void ath11k_reg_restore_user_cc(struct ath11k *ar);
 #endif
